# Divisi - the string ensemble: twelve top oscillators divided down in
# octaves, keys gated into six registers (violin, viola, cello, contrabass,
# choir and brass), one shared envelope or one per note, then a thick chorus
# and a phaser.
#
# Each patch plays the `pad` phrase, four held chords, except the brass
# patches, which play `chord`. 64 patches in six families: strings, low,
# choir, brass, layers and motion.
#
# Levels: every patch is levelled by `volume` to about -29.5 on `loud`, one
# note at its own note. A chord of four reads about 6 dB louder. Patches with
# a slow attack read lower, since a single note never reaches full in the
# measured window. The choir is even across the keyboard and the vowels, so a
# choir patch reads the same on any note. Violin and viola peak about 15 dB
# over their rms, so a big chord at full velocity can still peak near full
# scale; the master's limiter takes that.
#
# Every patch but Init carries eight named macros. Destinations are numbered
# as in Divisi.h's MacroDest: #1 violin, #2 viola, #3 cello, #4 contrabass,
# #5 choir, #6 vowel, #7 brass, #8 sweep, #9 brass decay, #10 blat, #11 tone,
# #12 attack, #13 release, #14 ensemble, #15 speed, #16 phaser, #17 rate,
# #18 feedback, #19 velocity, #20 volume, #21 pitch (24 semitones a unit).
# The set is the same on every patch: Bright, Swell, Longer, Lush, Voices,
# Brass, Phase and Low. A macro whose knob has no room left goes the other way
# under the opposite name (Dark, Sharper, Shorter, Drier, Light, ...), and a
# patch already full of choir or brass gets Vowel or Blat in its place. Where
# a macro at full moves the level by more than 1.2 dB, a volume route takes it
# back out.
#
# Values are in each parameter's own units; `audition params Divisi` lists
# them. A patch names only what it changes.

machine Divisi
role    pad

# --- strings ------------------------------------------------------------------

patch Init family=strings note=60 range=36..84

patch "Full Strings" family=strings note=60 range=36..84
  # Violins, violas and cellos, a little more chorus.
  set macro1 "Bright"
  set macro2 "Swell"
  set macro3 "Longer"
  set macro4 "Drier"
  set macro5 "Voices"
  set macro6 "Brass"
  set macro7 "Phase"
  set macro8 "Low"
  mac1_d1  #11
  mac1_a1  0.35
  mac2_d1  #12
  mac2_a1  0.2
  mac3_d1  #13
  mac3_a1  0.2
  mac4_d1  #14
  mac4_a1  -0.5
  mac4_d2  #20
  mac4_a2  -0.153
  mac5_d1  #5
  mac5_a1  0.5
